# TEMPLATE ONLY. Copy to hotends.cfg after verifying every delivered heater and
# thermistor. Include hardware.cfg with the M8P V1.1 pin profile first.
# The planned kits are 24 V/48 W with 100K 3950 NTC sensors; the actual delivered
# parts are not confirmed. Replace every sensor_type below with its verified
# Klipper type (Generic 3950 only if the sensor specification matches).
# The 4700-ohm pull-up assumes verified ordinary NTC inputs and matching jumpers.
# Set nozzle_diameter to the actual fitted nozzle (0.4 mm is the project default).
# 300 C is a ceiling, not approval to exceed the installed hotend's rated limit.
# T0-T3 heater pins drive external DC switch CONTROL inputs, not the new PSU
# directly; see wiring-plan.md. Selected switches must support the default
# Klipper 0.100 s (10 Hz) heater PWM cycle, or a deliberately reviewed cycle.

# The candidate printer.cfg retains the SB2209 RP2040 motor pins. Complete its
# required HGX gear ratio, rotation distance and motor settings before use.
# Remove its old heater/sensor/control/PID/temperature-limit definitions before
# adding this thermal overlay; reconcile any old extruder SAVE_CONFIG values.
# Do not delete unrelated bed, probe or motion calibration. Do not copy the
# upstream Trident motor or printer sections into the Voron configuration.
# extruder1..5 deliberately have no motor or stepper-driver definitions.

# WATERMARK IS TEMPORARY FOR INITIAL HEATER/PID COMMISSIONING ONLY.
# Verify one heater/sensor pair at a time, run PID_CALIBRATE for each heater at
# an appropriate verified operating temperature, and record its measured gains.
# Before enabling printing, replace each control: watermark with control: pid
# plus that heater's measured pid_Kp/pid_Ki/pid_Kd. Save the file and RESTART.
# No sample PID values are supplied. If using SAVE_CONFIG instead of entering
# the measured values here, remove the corresponding control/PID options from
# this include before SAVE_CONFIG; otherwise Klipper reports an include conflict.
# Do not enable simultaneous heating until the full wiring/power budget passes.

[extruder]
nozzle_diameter: 0.4
filament_diameter: 1.75
heater_pin: CX_T0_HEATER
sensor_pin: CX_T0_SENSOR
sensor_type: REPLACE_WITH_VERIFIED_SENSOR_TYPE
pullup_resistor: 4700
min_temp: 0
max_temp: 300
min_extrude_temp: 180
control: watermark

